# Sanaro's stage N15 (docs/sanaro.md section 24): a radar that sweeps longer. pc-sanaro-n11 (PR #662)
# found that holding fire costs 7 to 11 points of survival. Gun heat drives the radar: below LOCK (0.9)
# every scan flips it onto the target, above it the radar sweeps. Never firing kept the radar locked,
# and the anti-gravity lost sight of the robots closing in. So the field view, not the gun, is where
# survival lives. These arms lower LOCK so that the radar sweeps for longer after each shot.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-sanaro-n12        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-sanaro-n12)
# Run it from master:
#   git checkout master && git pull
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers. Every step resumes; no step needs
# a decision. Nothing here touches Hadur, Saor, TwinSaor, Deise, JayLexi or Eveimear. No teach run.
#
# Why it should win: a shot heats the gun to 1.02 to 1.6, and it cools 0.1 a tick. With LOCK 0.9 the
# radar sweeps for only 1 to 7 ticks after a shot, then sits on one robot for 9 ticks. n11 showed
# what a radar that never sweeps costs (-2 to -4.4 APS). Sweeping for longer should buy back some of
# that view of the field. n03 tested the other way, LOCK 1.0, which locks sooner, and lost 1.72. So the
# slope runs this way. Every arm costs 0 bytes (LOCK is one constant) and fits at 249 B. Melee cards
# may be field-wide (Leigh, 2026-11-03 22:18).
#
# Arms (sanaro-arms/arms.txt, on 0.4's source):
#   S4  Sanaro 0.4 as banked (control, 249 B)
#   K7  LOCK 0.7: two more sweep ticks after each shot
#   K5  LOCK 0.5: four more
#   K3  LOCK 0.3: six more, locking only in the last three ticks before the gun is cool
# Live-shaped census: 43 fields x 20 fresh seeds (base 30000) = 860 battles an arm, about 45 min an
# arm at n11's 1,150 an hour. About 3 h in all, the pilot included.
# Pilot (Leigh's rule, 2026-11-03): the first 4 of the 20 seeds of every arm (172 battles an arm,
# 20% of the run, about 36 min). sanaro_read --stop-below 0 then stops the card and opens the
# results PR unless some arm reads at or above S4. The full steps resume the pilot's battles.
# Read against S4. An arm passes when the low end of its difference is above zero (SANARO-13). A
# passing arm is 0.5 on Leigh's word.
# Stop rules on every battle step (docs/bench/watch.md; halt, every battle fought is kept and a
# rerun resumes):
# - 20 failed battles (a broken jar).
# - No battle in 30 minutes (a hung step).
# - 40+ skipped turns a battle over the last 100 (the PR #331 build-up).
# - The pilot gate above (exit 3 ends the card with a results PR).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on a stop.

set MVN = mvn -q -Drobocode.version=1.11.1 compile exec:java
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin
set ARMS = S4,K7,K5,K3
set W = work/sanaro-n12

prep | (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests install -pl sanaro -am) && mkdir -p ${W} && cp ../sanaro/target/hadur117.nano.Sanaro_0.4.jar opponents/ && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set nanomelee-field.txt && for f in melee-census-317/f*.txt; do ./fetch-opponents.sh --set "$f" || exit 1; done

arms | SANARO_RUN=n12 bash tools/sanaro_arms.sh live 20 30000 ${ARMS} && for a in S4 K7 K5 K3; do sed '/^--seeds$/{n;s/.*/4/;}' ${W}/live-$a.args > ${W}/pilot-$a.args || exit 1; done
  after: prep

pilot-S4 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/pilot-S4.args"
  after: arms
  watch: battles=172
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

pilot-K7 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/pilot-K7.args"
  after: pilot-S4
  watch: battles=172
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

pilot-K5 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/pilot-K5.args"
  after: pilot-K7
  watch: battles=172
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

pilot-K3 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/pilot-K3.args"
  after: pilot-K5
  watch: battles=172
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

pilot | python3 tools/sanaro_read.py --work-root ${W} --field live --arms ${ARMS} --control S4 --only ${W}/live/micro.txt --live 66.44 --stop-below 0 > ${OUT}/sanaro-n12-pilot.md; rc=$?; if [ $rc -eq 3 ]; then bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-sanaro-n12-results "Sanaro stage N15: a radar that sweeps longer (stopped at the pilot)" ${OUT}/sanaro-n12-pilot.md; fi; exit $rc
  after: pilot-K3

live-S4 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/live-S4.args"
  after: pilot
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-K7 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/live-K7.args"
  after: live-S4
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-K5 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/live-K5.args"
  after: live-K7
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

live-K3 | ${MVN} "-Dexec.args=@${W}/live-K3.args"
  after: live-K5
  watch: battles=860
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: skips 40 over 100

read-live | python3 tools/sanaro_read.py --work-root ${W} --field live --arms ${ARMS} --control S4 --only ${W}/live/micro.txt --live 66.44 > ${OUT}/sanaro-n12-live.md
  after: live-K3

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-sanaro-n12-results "Sanaro stage N15: a radar that sweeps longer, against 0.4" ${OUT}/sanaro-n12-pilot.md ${OUT}/sanaro-n12-live.md ${OUT}/sanaro-n12-live-*.md
  after: read-live
